PARSFILE Sensors_Traffic\Traffic\TMotion_dfeaed58-b113-465f-b7ee-2eff121a6c4c.par
#BlueLink5 Multiple Moving Objects`1 Vehicle, Stopped On Hwy` Traffic Vehicles (Forward)` , Link 6`TMotion_dfeaed58-b113-465f-b7ee-2eff121a6c4c






#EMBEDDED_NOTES
#This is a simple ACC test where the lead vehicle is moving at constant speed on the highway, initially out-of-range of the ego vehicle's ACC radar
#- Once the lead vehicle is in-range and detected by the ACC radar, the ego vehicle ACC slows to match the speed of the lead vehicle, and creeps to the desired minimum spacing distance
#
#An additional moving vehicle is in the adjacent lane and traveling at a constant speed, near the ego and lead vehicle, to assure that ACC Radar of the ego vehicle does not process a false detection, which could result in erroneous braking
#
#The lateral positions of the moving objects are set using the LTARG function, with datasets specified with ILTARG. Descriptions are specified that will appear in the Echo file. A new command SET_ILTARG_FOR_ID adds LTARG datasets.
#END_EMBEDDED_NOTES

LOG_ENTRY Used Dataset: Generic Data Group; { ADAS: Traffic for ACC & FCW } Traffic: ACC, Slow Down Test
